---
import fs from 'node:fs';
import path from 'node:path';
import { getCollection, render } from 'astro:content';
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import KitFlow from '../components/diagrams/KitFlow.astro';

// Read at build time; astro build runs with the site directory as cwd.
const gateSource = fs.readFileSync(path.join(process.cwd(), '../scripts/gate.sh'), 'utf8');

/** The gate's own section banners are the honest list of what it checks. */
const sections = [...gateSource.matchAll(/^# -+ (.+)$/gm)].map((match) => match[1].trim());
const requiredCount = (() => {
  const block = gateSource.match(/required=\(([\s\S]*?)\)/);
  const listed = block ? block[1].trim().split('\n').length : 0;
  const generated = [...gateSource.matchAll(/required\+=\(/g)].length;
  return { listed, generated };
})();

const checks = [
  {
    name: 'Structure',
    detail:
      'Every method page, phase prompt, skill, checklist and example ADR is a required file. The old gate could pass with method/ deleted.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Skills and symlinks',
    detail: '.claude/skills and .grok/skills must resolve to .agents/skills, so every tool sees the same three project skills.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Template naming',
    detail:
      'No live CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md or GROK.md inside kit/ or an example packet — an agent operating the playbook would load a take-home phase plan as its own rules.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Placeholders',
    detail: 'A filled example may not contain a TODO: line or a | TODO table row. Filled means filled.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Links',
    detail: 'Every relative markdown link resolves on disk. Broken cross-references are how a cascade rots quietly.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Forbidden terms',
    detail:
      'Structural bans live in scripts/forbidden-terms.txt. Personal names go in an untracked local list: a committed denylist of names publishes the names it exists to keep out.',
  },
  {
    name: 'copy-kit smoke',
    detail:
      'A real copy into a temporary directory must produce the renamed agent files, the checklist, and a README that still carries the fill order.',
  },
];

const agents = (await getCollection('root')).find((entry) => entry.id.toLowerCase() === 'agents');
const contributing = (await getCollection('root')).find(
  (entry) => entry.id.toLowerCase() === 'contributing'
);
const agentsRendered = agents ? await render(agents) : null;
const contributingRendered = contributing ? await render(contributing) : null;
---

<Doc
  title="Repository machinery"
  description="The gate that must pass before a commit, what copy-kit.sh moves into a working tree, and the rules an agent operating this repository has to follow."
  eyebrow="Reference"
  source="scripts/gate.sh"
  headings={[
    { depth: 2, slug: 'the-gate', text: 'The gate' },
    { depth: 2, slug: 'copy-kit', text: 'copy-kit.sh' },
    { depth: 2, slug: 'agent-files', text: 'Agent files' },
    { depth: 2, slug: 'contributing', text: 'Contributing' },
  ]}
>
  <p>
    This repository argues that an objective checklist beats "it runs". It has to hold itself to
    that, so the routine has a gate of its own — one script, run before every commit, that fails
    on anything the documentation claims but the tree does not deliver.
  </p>

  <pre><code>./scripts/gate.sh</code></pre>

  <h2 id="the-gate">What the gate checks</h2>
  <p class="counts">
    <span><b>{requiredCount.listed}</b> paths listed explicitly</span>
    <span><b>{requiredCount.generated}</b> generated groups (steps, prompts, skills, ADRs)</span>
    <span><b>{sections.length}</b> check sections</span>
  </p>

  <dl class="checks not-prose">
    {
      checks.map((check) => (
        <div class="check">
          <dt>{check.name}</dt>
          <dd>{check.detail}</dd>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </dl>

  <Callout kind="stop">
    <p>
      Do not weaken the forbidden list, and do not delete a required file to make the gate green.
      If you deliberately add or remove a method page, a prompt, a skill, or an ADR, update the
      lists in <code>scripts/gate.sh</code> in the same commit.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2 id="copy-kit">copy-kit.sh</h2>
  <p>
    The kit is copied, never cloned as a submission. The script refuses a non-empty destination,
    renames the agent templates, and records which playbook commit produced the tree.
  </p>

  <Figure caption="What travels into a working tree, what is renamed, what is generated, and what stays in the playbook.">
    <KitFlow />
  </Figure>

  <h2 id="agent-files">Agent files</h2>
  <p>
    <code>AGENTS.md</code> is the canonical instruction file for every agent that operates this
    repository; <code>CLAUDE.md</code> and <code>GROK.md</code> point at it and hold no rules of
    their own.
  </p>
  {agentsRendered && (
    <details class="embed">
      <summary>AGENTS.md in full</summary>
      <div class="embed-body">
        <agentsRendered.Content />
      </div>
    </details>
  )}

  <h2 id="contributing">Contributing</h2>
  {contributingRendered && (
    <details class="embed">
      <summary>CONTRIBUTING.md in full</summary>
      <div class="embed-body">
        <contributingRendered.Content />
      </div>
    </details>
  )}
</Doc>

<style>
  .counts {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-5);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--size-sm);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    border-block: var(--border-thin) solid var(--rule);
    padding-block: var(--space-3);
  }
  .counts b {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }

  .checks {
    margin: var(--space-5) 0 0;
    display: grid;
    border-top: var(--border-thin) solid var(--rule);
  }
  .check {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 12rem 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    padding: var(--space-3) 0;
    border-bottom: var(--border-thin) solid var(--rule);
  }
  .check dt {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--size-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .check dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--size-md);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: var(--leading-normal);
  }

  .embed {
    border: var(--border-thin) solid var(--rule);
    background: var(--sheet);
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }
  .embed summary {
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    cursor: pointer;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: var(--size-sm);
  }
  .embed-body {
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-4) var(--space-5);
    border-top: var(--border-thin) solid var(--rule);
  }
  .embed-body :global(h1) {
    display: none;
  }
  .embed-body :global(* + *) {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }

  @media (max-width: 44rem) {
    .check {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-1);
    }
  }
</style>
